sed's comma range on a file that exists is refused with the form `lets` reads. The second call is
the control: no prefix of `nope.ts` names a file, so the not-found text is the plain one.

```console
$ lets show a.ts:40,60
? 1
a.ts:40,60: no such file · did you mean a.ts:40-60
ERROR_CODE=not_found

$ lets show nope.ts
? 1
nope.ts: No such file or directory (os error 2)
ERROR_CODE=not_found

```
